WEBVTT

﻿1

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:37.079
SNAPPER FILMS
Presents


00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:44.999
A Film By
JUHA WUOLIJOKI


00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:48.839
You all know who I am.


00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:53.679
We meet once a year,
on Christmas Eve.


00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:00.079
But children and adults,
young and old:


00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:05.319
I, too, have been a child.
You don't believe it?


00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:07.959
Let me tell you a story.


00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:15.359
CHRISTMAS STORY


00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:35.599
Nikolas... Dear Nikolas.


00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:40.559
Aada has a high fever. We'll have to
take her to the village.


00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:47.119
The firewood should last
until we return.


00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:53.239
We'll be back when the little hand
and the big hand are like that.


00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:58.039
We'll save time by
taking a shortcut through the ice.


00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:03.399
Nikolas, you can finish Aada's
present while waiting. Right?


00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:15.679
Where did you get the idea
of giving presents at Christmas?


00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.879
Although it's a nice idea.


00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:49.119
Nikolas, we found your parents'
tracks on the ice.


00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:54.519
The tracks lead straight
into open water.


00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:01.879
I'm so sorry.


00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:03.519
Nobody wants to see an orphaned boy
starve or freeze to death.


00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:08.679
Of course not.
-We already have three children.


00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:11.159
It's the same thing with everybody.


00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:16.239
Fishermen's wives know how hard it
is to make a living. And Nikolas...


00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:21.079
Why don't you cast him
into the lake with his family?


00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:26.959
I can do that,
if none of you is man enough.


00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:33.439
He scurried off. The little runt
has no sense of humour.


00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:41.559
I have an idea.


00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:45.399
Kristiina and I
can take care of him for a while.


00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:50.999
I've had fisherman's luck lately.
We have some savings.


00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:56.999
I believe that we can feed an extra
mouth. At least through the winter.


00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:01.879
I think that the whole village
should take care of the boy.


00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:07.279
How many households
do we have here?


00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:12.599
Four, five, six.


00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:19.439
Each household shall take
care of the boy for a year -


00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:22.639
and then send him to the next house.


00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:26.239
I think that we can manage that.


00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:30.039
I'm not going to take part
in that nonsense.


00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:34.399
You don't live here, Iisakki.
It's not of your concern.


00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.799
Quit your yapping.


00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:48.599
We'll all take care of Nikolas.


00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:52.239
Beginning with the Hannuses.


00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:56.359
The boy will move to the next family
on Christmas.


00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:00.399
Is this agreed?
-Yes.


00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:02.879
Good.


00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:10.719
Merry Christmas, sister Aada.


00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:41.679
I could not forget
my mother and my father -


00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:44.959
and my sister Aada.


00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:48.399
I knew they would not be
coming back -


00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:51.559
but I missed them dearly.


00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:12.999
Thank you.


00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:37.359
But time heals the wounds -


00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:41.919
and by autumn
the sadness began to fade away.


00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:51.359
My boat's broken. Fix it.
-Ask your father.


00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:55.879
My father has gone fishing.
-Ask your mother, then.


00:08:56.240 --> 00:09:00.639
Mother can't do it.
-Give it to me.


00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.199
Turn, boat!
-It won't turn!


00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:17.799
Why doesn't it come here?
Turn right!


00:09:22.280 --> 00:09:24.239
There it goes!


00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:43.919
I didn't know it back then -


00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:49.119
but Eemeli would become
a good friend. My best friend.


00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:52.719
Good throw.
It bounced off the water.


00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:58.199
I found a great stone.
-Stretch your arm back and throw.


00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.679
You can do it.
One, two, three!


00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:17.399
Let's get another one.


00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:29.279
Then came the moment
I had been dreading.


00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:34.199
I had to move to another
family for the very first time.


00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:40.119
Are you sure
you'll find your way to the Heinos?


00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:43.279
Bye bye.
-Bye bye.


00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:14.599
Years, families and Christmases
came and went.


00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:18.319
Every Christmas I carved presents -


00:11:18.680 --> 00:11:22.039
for the children
of my former families.


00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:25.799
As the years passed,
there were so many of them -


00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:33.199
that I had to deliver the presents
to their front doors at night.


00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:37.039
It suited me fine -


00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:40.559
because I didn't want to make
a great fuss about it.


00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:42.919
Instead, I acted ignorant -


00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:48.039
if someone came to thank me
after Christmas.


00:11:58.680 --> 00:12:02.519
On my sixth year,
not everything went as planned.


00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:05.519
That year was hard
for the whole village.


00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:09.479
Early frost wiped out
almost the entire crop.


00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:13.599
It was like the lake
was empty of fish that year.


00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:39.599
No fish today either?
-That's right, Hilla.


00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:41.919
That's a pity.


00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:45.599
If things didn't turn
for the better -


00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:50.599
no family would be able
to house me for the winter.


00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:40.959
Eemeli? What is it?


00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:43.999
It's Mad Iisakki. Run away!


00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:55.319
Get your homes in shipshape
for Christmas!


00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:59.079
Scoops, ladles, cups!


00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:06.479
Spatulas, tubs and potato mashers!
I have everything you need here!


00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:10.599
And if I don't have it,
it can be made to order!


00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:16.959
Boy, come here.


00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:28.879
You haven't bought this from me.


00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:35.479
Are you buying things from other
carpenters instead of Iisakki?


00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:41.079
A bad year. We have no money.
We can barely feed ourselves.


00:14:41.640 --> 00:14:44.559
Where did you buy this?
Answer me!


00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:48.999
I made it myself.
-Don't lie, whippersnapper.


00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:54.959
And whose boy are you?
-Nobody's.


00:14:56.280 --> 00:15:02.599
Oh yeah, you're the poor devil who
is going around from house to house.


00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:08.959
Where are the others?
-At the village meeting.


00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:14.279
What is so important
that they must have a meeting?


00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:18.159
They're deciding what to do with me.
They can't afford me.


00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:21.279
No wonder.
You must be such a glutton -


00:15:21.640 --> 00:15:25.559
that you have ruined the village.
And now I can't sell anything.


00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:29.359
You should've been cast
into the lake. Get lost!


00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:44.079
But why? You don't like children.
-He can help me at work.


00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:47.919
We know you, Iisakki.


00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:54.599
I was planning to shape that brat
into a man within a year -


00:15:54.960 --> 00:16:00.199
but if my offer isn't good enough
for you, there's nothing I can do.


00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:02.679
Wait, Iisakki.


00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:08.559
Maybe...
Maybe we should consider it.


00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:12.799
There's nothing to consider.
He'll be better off with me -


00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:18.119
than starving to death
here in this poor village. Right?


00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:42.719
This might be the last time
I can visit you.


00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:46.439
Iisakki lives so far away.


00:16:51.560 --> 00:16:53.919
Merry Christmas, little Aada.


00:17:13.520 --> 00:17:15.759
Nikolas, come and see!


00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:23.559
Nikolas.


00:17:25.720 --> 00:17:30.919
It's been six years since
you were orphaned and came to us.


00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:37.919
At first I was sorry that we
couldn't find you a family -


00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:40.679
to take you in.


00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:49.119
You had to go around from household
to household, one year at a time.


00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:56.559
But now I believe that none of us
have regretted it.


00:17:57.920 --> 00:18:00.719
We all have gotten to know you.


00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:06.799
And so, in a way,
you are our child.


00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:09.519
And our brother.


00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:14.439
On behalf of all the villagers,
especially the children -


00:18:14.800 --> 00:18:18.959
we want to give you
a little memento.


00:18:25.880 --> 00:18:28.759
I can't...
-Of course you can.


00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:31.439
The sledge belongs to you.


00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:41.439
Are you still loafing about?
Get in the sleigh.


00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:44.599
Or you can walk the whole way.


00:19:45.840 --> 00:19:48.799
You're not going to cry, are you?


00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:54.359
Hilma, trot along home
before night falls.


00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:11.999
What are you gawking at?
Take Hilma into the stall.


00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:15.439
I'll go inside and light the stove.


00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:18.919
And leave this sledge in the stall.


00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:24.119
No mucking about here.
You came here to work. Get up!


00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:44.079
And you sleep there.
-But...


00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:48.559
No buts!
Did you forget whose house this is?


00:20:48.920 --> 00:20:51.719
And you will call me master.
-Yes.


00:20:52.080 --> 00:20:53.839
What?
-Yes, master.


00:20:54.200 --> 00:20:57.039
Good. Your name is Brat.


00:20:57.400 --> 00:21:02.119
It suits you better than Nikolas.
Take your bags in there. Move it!


00:21:35.240 --> 00:21:38.479
Wake up, Brat. Get to work.


00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:52.479
Let's get to the workshop.
You go on ahead.


00:21:53.960 --> 00:21:57.759
Where's the workshop?
-You're standing on it.


00:22:34.280 --> 00:22:36.479
What do you think?


00:22:40.840 --> 00:22:42.959
Take a look at this dresser.


00:22:43.320 --> 00:22:46.919
The secret is in the wooden inlays.


00:22:47.920 --> 00:22:50.799
It's made of maple.
This is how I make money.


00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:54.719
Scoops and ladles
are child's play compared to this.


00:22:55.160 --> 00:22:59.599
These will go to parsons, gentleman
farmers and other wealthy people.


00:22:59.960 --> 00:23:05.799
This will go to a judge.
-Is this chair going there too?


00:23:07.560 --> 00:23:10.639
It's made of pine,
this is made of maple.


00:23:11.880 --> 00:23:14.839
Don't you recognise timber species?


00:23:15.240 --> 00:23:18.879
Maybe I made a mistake.
You're no good as a carpenter.


00:23:20.560 --> 00:23:24.239
You haven't made a mistake, master.
I'm a quick learner.


00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:29.639
A quick learner, eh? Let's see
how quickly you learn to tidy up.


00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:32.159
Get on with it.


00:23:35.280 --> 00:23:38.399
Where are you going?
-Upstairs.


00:23:39.160 --> 00:23:42.919
You don't need to go upstairs
to tidy up the workshop.


00:23:44.320 --> 00:23:46.759
There's no need to clean up here...


00:23:49.440 --> 00:23:51.919
The workbench is covered with dust.


00:23:52.560 --> 00:23:57.359
If it gets mixed with varnish or
stain, the whole work is ruined.


00:23:58.280 --> 00:23:59.839
Lesson number one:


00:24:00.200 --> 00:24:05.039
The workshop will be kept tidy
at all times, no matter what.


00:24:05.560 --> 00:24:09.359
Lesson number two:
Hand me your sheath-knife.


00:24:13.880 --> 00:24:16.599
You don't use this on my timber.


00:24:17.280 --> 00:24:20.359
Don't!
-What?


00:24:21.480 --> 00:24:24.079
It was my father's.


00:24:27.120 --> 00:24:30.119
Take a decent sheath-knife
from there.


00:25:54.200 --> 00:25:56.319
Go to bed.


00:25:59.480 --> 00:26:02.359
Remember to snuff out the candles.


00:26:31.360 --> 00:26:34.279
Why?
-It has no branches.


00:27:22.240 --> 00:27:24.879
How can I find my things now?


00:28:29.080 --> 00:28:31.039
Master...


00:28:32.360 --> 00:28:35.439
A year has passed
and I have to go soon -


00:28:35.800 --> 00:28:39.799
so I thought that I would
thank all the villagers.


00:28:41.000 --> 00:28:45.999
Maybe I could take a day off?
-No.


00:28:46.360 --> 00:28:47.879
When time is pressing -


00:28:48.240 --> 00:28:51.799
you don't waste time thinking,
you work harder.


00:28:57.960 --> 00:29:00.239
A day off eh?


00:29:19.320 --> 00:29:23.799
What are you doing here?
Why aren't you in bed?


00:29:29.760 --> 00:29:34.999
Have you stolen timber from me?
-You threw it away, master.


00:29:35.600 --> 00:29:38.639
So this is what you do
behind my back.


00:29:46.000 --> 00:29:47.839
I'm sorry, master.


00:29:54.080 --> 00:29:57.599
It isn't badly broken.


00:29:59.200 --> 00:30:02.319
Bring me the wood drill
and a headless nail.


00:30:02.680 --> 00:30:07.279
Why are you working in the dark?
It only results in duds and rejects.


00:30:12.760 --> 00:30:14.679
There.


00:30:22.480 --> 00:30:24.679
Now you can't tell it's broken.


00:30:26.480 --> 00:30:29.599
You have more toys
somewhere, right?


00:30:44.240 --> 00:30:47.319
You must really like
those little brats.


00:30:47.680 --> 00:30:50.319
Did you plan to slip out
to deliver presents -


00:30:50.680 --> 00:30:56.239
because I didn't give you a day off?
That's what I thought.


00:30:58.320 --> 00:31:00.159
Go on then -


00:31:00.520 --> 00:31:03.919
but remember
to return before sunrise.


00:31:04.280 --> 00:31:08.159
We don't idle away,
even though it's Christmas.


00:31:22.440 --> 00:31:26.039
Master...
-Not a word. I may change my mind.


00:31:26.920 --> 00:31:30.799
You can build your toys
in the evenings.


00:31:31.960 --> 00:31:35.719
I might even help you.
At least now I can get some sleep.


00:31:36.080 --> 00:31:40.599
Building toys in the middle
of the night... Humbug!


00:31:54.760 --> 00:32:00.919
Finally you showed up. I thought
you had gone into hibernation.


00:32:01.480 --> 00:32:04.919
I already put your junk
in the sleigh.


00:32:08.160 --> 00:32:10.039
What are you gawking at?


00:32:10.400 --> 00:32:13.319
You wouldn't have made it back
before sunrise.


00:32:13.680 --> 00:32:17.639
The last workday would
have gone to waste. Hop in.


00:32:21.120 --> 00:32:22.919
Let's go.


00:32:38.120 --> 00:32:44.879
That was the last house.
-This is foolishness.


00:32:45.240 --> 00:32:49.479
I can understand why you do this,
but an old man like me...


00:32:49.920 --> 00:32:52.879
Let's go home.
-There's one more place.


00:32:57.920 --> 00:33:01.679
Hold on. Show me that.


00:33:05.960 --> 00:33:12.359
I made a horse like this
when the boys were young.


00:33:13.520 --> 00:33:15.439
What boys?


00:33:15.920 --> 00:33:21.439
I had two boys, Hermanni and Henrik.


00:33:23.160 --> 00:33:29.839
And a wife, Marget. She died when
the boys were about your age.


00:33:32.160 --> 00:33:35.919
Then they went to sea
and left me all alone -


00:33:36.280 --> 00:33:38.839
because I had become like this.


00:33:41.000 --> 00:33:45.079
I see Henrik and Hermanni
in all children.


00:33:46.200 --> 00:33:49.479
That's why I'm mean
to children.


00:33:51.160 --> 00:33:54.359
I still miss my boys.


00:33:59.360 --> 00:34:04.839
What I mean to say is...
You could stay with me.


00:34:12.960 --> 00:34:15.239
Merry Christmas, Nikolas.


00:34:25.920 --> 00:34:30.679
My father's sheath-knife.
Thank you, master.


00:34:31.800 --> 00:34:36.439
From now on you can call me Iisakki.


00:34:45.200 --> 00:34:49.599
Merry Christmas, Aada.
-Merry Christmas, Aada.


00:34:52.200 --> 00:34:58.559
Merry Christmas, Iisakki.
-Merry Christmas, Nikolas.


00:35:01.520 --> 00:35:03.799
That's enough. Let's go.


00:35:07.960 --> 00:35:13.799
That Christmas changed everything.
The village overcame the bad years.


00:35:14.160 --> 00:35:17.279
My vagabond life was over.


00:35:17.680 --> 00:35:23.159
Iisakki provided me a home
that I didn't have to give up.


00:35:48.800 --> 00:35:52.999
Thank you very much.
Good day to you.


00:35:53.360 --> 00:35:55.959
Hurry up!


00:35:56.640 --> 00:35:58.799
Good day to you.


00:36:02.360 --> 00:36:05.639
Come and buy a dresser!


00:36:48.520 --> 00:36:51.559
The years with Iisakki
passed quickly.


00:36:54.200 --> 00:36:59.959
Before I knew it, I was all
grown up, with a beard and all.


00:37:23.600 --> 00:37:29.799
The village had grown.
There were so many new children -


00:37:30.480 --> 00:37:33.719
that me and Iisakki
could not keep count.


00:37:37.600 --> 00:37:40.039
But we had a secret helper.


00:38:10.360 --> 00:38:13.839
Nikolas.
-Eemeli.


00:38:14.680 --> 00:38:18.679
Long time no see.
You should come more often.


00:38:19.040 --> 00:38:22.319
I've been busy.
Iisakki is no longer young.


00:38:22.680 --> 00:38:25.199
Do you have the list?


00:38:35.320 --> 00:38:39.279
Well, I'll be...
So many new children.


00:38:40.360 --> 00:38:46.599
As a matter of fact, one name is
missing from that list. Elsa?


00:38:53.280 --> 00:38:56.239
Is that...
-A girl, three months.


00:38:56.800 --> 00:38:59.359
Let's add her to the list.


00:39:00.200 --> 00:39:03.519
What is the name
of this little princess?


00:39:04.440 --> 00:39:06.279
Aada.


00:39:09.080 --> 00:39:10.759
Aada?


00:39:17.360 --> 00:39:20.719
Hello, Aada.


00:39:47.640 --> 00:39:54.279
Nikolas, meet Henrik and Hermanni.


00:39:54.760 --> 00:39:56.479
My sons.


00:39:59.280 --> 00:40:03.999
I sought them out
and asked them here.


00:40:05.080 --> 00:40:06.799
Yes...


00:40:09.960 --> 00:40:12.759
We were wrong when we...


00:40:13.720 --> 00:40:16.719
We want to make it up
to our father.


00:40:17.480 --> 00:40:22.759
We came to take him to live with us.
-To live with you? Where?


00:40:23.120 --> 00:40:28.759
Away from here. Father is too old
to be living in arctic conditions.


00:40:29.640 --> 00:40:31.319
What about me?


00:40:31.680 --> 00:40:37.719
You'll get the house and
the workshop. You've earned them.


00:40:39.960 --> 00:40:42.119
Wait, Nikolas.


00:40:52.440 --> 00:40:54.319
Nikolas...


00:41:03.520 --> 00:41:07.839
Nikolas, try to understand.


00:41:08.840 --> 00:41:13.399
Even though I love you
like my own son...


00:41:19.000 --> 00:41:23.639
This key opens the chest
under my bed.


00:41:26.440 --> 00:41:30.959
I've always been skimpy,
maybe too much so.


00:41:32.240 --> 00:41:34.639
I think you can do better.


00:41:36.320 --> 00:41:41.519
Try to understand.


00:43:59.400 --> 00:44:01.319
Nikolas.


00:44:08.560 --> 00:44:10.799
Eemeli.
-Nikolas.


00:44:11.160 --> 00:44:13.079
Hello.
-Hello.


00:44:17.200 --> 00:44:19.719
Where have you been?
-Here.


00:44:21.160 --> 00:44:24.199
Here! But everything is unfinished.


00:44:24.560 --> 00:44:27.359
These should last for ten years.


00:44:27.720 --> 00:44:30.639
This is barely enough
for next Christmas.


00:44:31.400 --> 00:44:33.559
What is that?
-A map.


00:44:34.960 --> 00:44:39.479
There, there... To this remote
village, to these houses.


00:44:39.840 --> 00:44:44.199
There, there, there, there, there...
Christmas presents.


00:44:44.560 --> 00:44:46.159
Christmas presents?
-Yes.


00:44:46.520 --> 00:44:51.159
So many villages and children.
How do you know who'll get what?


00:44:51.520 --> 00:44:53.399
There's a simple way.
-What is it?


00:44:53.760 --> 00:44:56.239
I shall write names on the wrapping.


00:44:57.080 --> 00:44:59.519
Wrapping?
-Ingenious, isn't it?


00:45:00.240 --> 00:45:02.679
How is all this possible?


00:45:10.280 --> 00:45:12.959
Iisakki's life savings.


00:45:14.080 --> 00:45:17.079
Now I can bring Christmas cheer
to the children.


00:45:17.440 --> 00:45:21.319
Nobody can live just for Christmas.


00:45:23.600 --> 00:45:27.919
I've been selfish. I've only brought
presents to those -


00:45:28.280 --> 00:45:31.079
who have helped me.
-Selfish?


00:45:31.800 --> 00:45:36.719
From now on, I'm going to appear
only on Christmas Eve. -Nikolas!


00:45:37.520 --> 00:45:39.599
I'll visit your shop once a year -


00:45:39.960 --> 00:45:43.319
to replenish my supplies and
to get a list of new children.


00:45:43.680 --> 00:45:46.799
There's more to life
than just Christmas.


00:45:49.600 --> 00:45:52.719
Like what?
-It's an impossible task.


00:45:54.240 --> 00:45:57.119
You don't have room
for all those presents.


00:45:57.480 --> 00:46:00.759
And Hilma won't be able
to pull the load.


00:46:03.760 --> 00:46:05.919
It can't be done.
-Yes, it can.


00:46:06.280 --> 00:46:09.759
Christmas is around the corner.
-Animals are quick to learn.


00:46:10.120 --> 00:46:13.599
Reindeer are not horses.
-Hilla, this is child's play.


00:46:13.960 --> 00:46:18.519
I can handle reindeer, dear.
"Reindeer, dear."


00:46:18.880 --> 00:46:20.599
You can try.


00:46:20.960 --> 00:46:25.519
Reindeer obey me better when
I'm wearing this colourful cap.


00:46:27.400 --> 00:46:31.759
Even the squirrels are afraid of
such a garish colour.


00:46:32.640 --> 00:46:36.559
Reindeer would obey me even
if I had a potholder on my head.


00:46:40.880 --> 00:46:44.439
I don't need any red caps.


00:46:48.960 --> 00:46:52.439
Okay, fall in line.
Put your antlers down.


00:46:54.040 --> 00:46:56.599
Come to Nikolas, chop-chop.


00:46:57.560 --> 00:47:01.559
Dasher, Dancer, Prancer and Blitzen,
your training begins.


00:47:01.920 --> 00:47:05.479
The first lesson... Lassoing.
Dancer, behave yourself.


00:47:05.840 --> 00:47:07.679
Sit there!


00:47:08.360 --> 00:47:11.559
Sit! Sit! Stay!


00:47:14.680 --> 00:47:19.759
Dasher, if you don't behave,
Nikolas will catch you! Prancer!


00:47:29.240 --> 00:47:31.359
Let's try again.


00:47:34.640 --> 00:47:36.719
Hold it!


00:47:39.000 --> 00:47:41.119
Dancer! Prancer!


00:48:01.840 --> 00:48:06.919
A red cap, a red coat...
And frieze trousers to boot.


00:48:08.480 --> 00:48:11.679
What was the colour?
-Red.


00:48:13.640 --> 00:48:16.119
Could you repeat that?


00:48:17.560 --> 00:48:19.559
Red!


00:48:22.160 --> 00:48:24.159
All right.


00:48:26.920 --> 00:48:28.959
I'll show you.


00:50:10.240 --> 00:50:14.199
Let's see, Aada.
What do you have there?


00:50:17.920 --> 00:50:20.719
A spinning top.
-That's nice.


00:50:24.480 --> 00:50:28.039
In a few years
the mysterious present-bearer -


00:50:28.400 --> 00:50:31.839
became the staple
of children's stories.


00:50:32.960 --> 00:50:37.399
Some swore to have seen elves
bringing presents at Christmas.


00:50:38.800 --> 00:50:43.519
Others claimed that the presents
were from a child-friendly gnome.


00:50:45.240 --> 00:50:47.959
Luckily, they didn't suspect me.


00:50:50.680 --> 00:50:54.039
Nikolas is coming!
-Run away!


00:51:04.040 --> 00:51:05.959
Good day.


00:51:10.240 --> 00:51:12.199
Hello, Aada.


00:51:14.840 --> 00:51:18.759
Where are the others?
-They are afraid of you.


00:51:22.440 --> 00:51:25.639
Me? Why?


00:51:28.480 --> 00:51:32.199
Mikko said that it's not you who
brings us presents at Christmas.


00:51:32.560 --> 00:51:38.719
That you hate children. Is it true?
-Mikko is half right.


00:51:39.920 --> 00:51:43.879
I don't bring presents.
But I don't hate children, either.


00:51:45.520 --> 00:51:47.759
Who brings the presents?


00:51:49.760 --> 00:51:55.639
Who knows?


00:52:04.360 --> 00:52:06.719
Nikolas told me when I asked him.


00:52:07.080 --> 00:52:10.839
Aada claims that you don't
bring us presents.


00:52:11.760 --> 00:52:13.639
Aada is right.


00:52:14.000 --> 00:52:15.639
Aada!


00:52:16.120 --> 00:52:18.839
Why did you say so?
Tell her the truth.


00:52:19.200 --> 00:52:24.319
No way. Children must not
associate me with the presents.


00:52:24.760 --> 00:52:27.759
It would ruin everything.
-Why is that?


00:52:28.120 --> 00:52:30.639
One day you'll understand.


00:52:45.360 --> 00:52:47.919
Nikolas!
-Eemeli?


00:52:48.480 --> 00:52:51.279
Is Aada here?
-No.


00:52:51.640 --> 00:52:54.039
Aada has gone missing.
-When?


00:52:57.640 --> 00:53:01.799
"Dear mother and father.
Don't worry. I went to find out -


00:53:02.640 --> 00:53:04.559
who brings all the presents."


00:53:04.920 --> 00:53:08.479
We have to wake everybody up
and arrange a search party.


00:53:08.840 --> 00:53:12.759
You must lend me some clothes.
Otherwise I'll be exposed.


00:53:14.720 --> 00:53:17.319
Okay, boys. Hurry on home.


00:53:24.400 --> 00:53:28.559
Let's form groups of two. A torch
and a lantern for each group.


00:53:29.480 --> 00:53:32.879
Aada couldn't have gone far.
Let's hurry.


00:53:33.360 --> 00:53:36.879
I know where she is.
-What did you say, Mikko?


00:53:37.240 --> 00:53:39.519
Aada wants to deliver you a present.


00:53:39.880 --> 00:53:45.679
Me? Why? -Aada doesn't believe
that you don't bring us presents.


00:53:46.040 --> 00:53:50.119
Why didn't you tell us earlier?
-I promised not to tell.


00:53:51.960 --> 00:53:54.079
Will Aada return?


00:53:57.600 --> 00:54:01.559
Aada!


00:54:01.920 --> 00:54:05.999
Aada doesn't know where you live.
And even if she knew -


00:54:06.360 --> 00:54:09.999
she won't be able to walk that far.
Aada!


00:54:17.160 --> 00:54:19.279
Aada!


00:55:16.600 --> 00:55:19.519
Nikolas?
-Aada!


00:55:26.920 --> 00:55:31.359
Nobody thought that you'd manage
to get this far.


00:55:32.320 --> 00:55:36.639
Twelve miles in a blizzard.
How is it possible?


00:55:37.440 --> 00:55:41.599
It was nothing on a reindeer sleigh.
-A reindeer sleigh?


00:55:42.520 --> 00:55:46.479
What reindeer sleigh?
-Suddenly, a sleigh appeared.


00:55:46.840 --> 00:55:51.479
I thought it was you but the sleigh
was empty... Well, not quite.


00:55:57.680 --> 00:56:02.639
I was cold so I put on your clothes.
Then the reindeer brought me here.


00:56:24.280 --> 00:56:29.319
I told Aada everything.
How I'd become the way I am -


00:56:29.760 --> 00:56:33.999
and why it was so important
to deliver presents at Christmas.


00:56:35.840 --> 00:56:40.679
I even revealed my dream
of continuing this tradition -


00:56:41.040 --> 00:56:43.599
when I would be gone.


00:56:45.960 --> 00:56:50.719
What kind of girl would Aada be now
if she hadn't become a water nymph?


00:56:51.720 --> 00:56:54.439
Hopefully she'd be like you.


00:57:01.600 --> 00:57:05.919
Merry Christmas, Aada.
-Merry Christmas, Aada.


00:57:08.240 --> 00:57:12.079
Merry Christmas, Aada.
-Merry Christmas, Nikolas.


00:57:45.200 --> 00:57:47.439
Aada kept her promise.


00:57:48.160 --> 00:57:51.799
She didn't reveal my secret.
Quite the opposite.


00:57:53.720 --> 00:57:59.199
He didn't look like Nikolas.
He was a wrinkly old man -


00:57:59.560 --> 00:58:02.319
who called himself Christmas Codger.


00:58:09.560 --> 00:58:13.559
The years passed,
and before I knew it -


00:58:13.960 --> 00:58:18.159
my friendship with Aada
had lasted almost twenty years.


00:58:20.960 --> 00:58:22.879
Nikolas!


00:58:30.440 --> 00:58:32.839
Well?
-I'm getting married.


00:58:39.720 --> 00:58:41.879
To Mikko?


00:59:04.240 --> 00:59:09.039
Nikolas, will you pick me up
on Christmas morning?


00:59:10.520 --> 00:59:12.719
Of course I will.


00:59:21.400 --> 00:59:23.799
Hello.
-Hello.


00:59:54.320 --> 00:59:57.399
Thank you.
-For what?


00:59:59.840 --> 01:00:01.999
For everything.


01:00:03.640 --> 01:00:05.599
Everything.


01:00:52.280 --> 01:00:54.559
My father is dead.


01:01:07.680 --> 01:01:14.599
Fear of losing love is part of love.
It's part of life.


01:01:16.880 --> 01:01:20.839
Your father...
Eemeli taught me that.


01:01:26.560 --> 01:01:29.719
You have taught me
how wonderful it is to give.


01:01:34.000 --> 01:01:35.799
Me?


01:01:36.800 --> 01:01:42.399
Nikolas, maybe you should
think of yourself for a change.


01:01:47.320 --> 01:01:49.519
Nothing lasts forever.


01:02:24.920 --> 01:02:28.279
It was time for me
to give in to my years.


01:02:29.440 --> 01:02:35.159
Next Christmas would be the last.
My last Christmas.


01:02:52.000 --> 01:02:54.559
It's beautiful. Who is it for?


01:02:56.720 --> 01:03:00.639
Can I gift wrap it?
-No. I want to do it myself.


01:03:02.760 --> 01:03:04.999
See you on Christmas morning.


01:03:20.160 --> 01:03:23.279
Are you sure you don't
want any help at Christmas?


01:03:23.640 --> 01:03:28.039
Yes. I want to do my rounds alone.


01:03:30.720 --> 01:03:36.439
Nikolas, remember your promise.
This is the last Christmas.


01:03:38.880 --> 01:03:41.199
This is the last Christmas.


01:05:26.960 --> 01:05:32.159
Nikolas?


01:06:04.120 --> 01:06:31.319
"Merry Christmas to little Aada.
Your brother, Nikolas."


01:06:31.680 --> 01:06:36.559
What is the meaning of this?
-We won't be seeing Nikolas again.


01:06:36.920 --> 01:06:43.439
What do you mean?
-I can't explain. I just know it.


01:07:06.120 --> 01:07:10.519
What are you doing?
There's no sense in doing that.


01:07:10.880 --> 01:07:13.399
Nikolas wanted this to continue.
-No.


01:07:13.760 --> 01:07:16.999
A present for our Nikolas
will disappoint other children.


01:07:17.360 --> 01:07:22.119
Other fathers have done this too...
-It's not the same thing.


01:07:24.320 --> 01:07:26.679
Mikko, that's cheating.


01:07:42.600 --> 01:07:45.399
Mikko?


01:08:28.040 --> 01:08:30.319
Merry Christmas, little Aada.


01:08:30.680 --> 01:08:33.239
Merry Christmas, Nikolas.


01:08:46.560 --> 01:08:50.519
Dasher, Dancer, Prancer and
Blitzen, ahoy!


01:09:13.840 --> 01:09:16.999
Merry Christmas!


